Turki bin Nasser Al Saud (14 April 1948 – 30 January 2021) was a Saudi prince, businessman and military officer. He was the head of the presidency of meteorology and environment in Saudi Arabia and a member of House of Saud. He was born in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia. Prince Turki began to serve as deputy commander at the Royal Saudi Air Force in 1996 and became a commander with the rank of general at the Force.
In November 2017, Saud was arrested in a corruption.
Turki bin Nasser died on 30 January 2021 in Riyadh, aged 72.

