Alla Yakovlevna Ioshpe (Yoshpe) (; 13 June 1937 – 30 January 2021) was a Soviet-Russian pop singer. She was honored with a People's Artist of the Russian Federation in 2002. She was born in Moscow. In 1960, at a university event, she met Stakhan Rakhimov. They formed a pop duo.
Yoshpe died on 30 January 2021 in Moscow, aged 83.

