Grant County is a county of the U.S. state of Arkansas. 17,958 people lived there at the 2020 census. The county seat is Sheridan. It was founded on February 4, 1869.

= = = Hempstead County, Arkansas = = =
Hempstead County is a county of the U.S. state of Arkansas. As of the 2020 census, the population was 20,065. The county seat is Hope. It was founded on December 15, 1818.

